{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's own GPS trace measures 19.71 km between the recorded pickup event and the recorded drop-off event, against a booked optimal route of 14.6 km. That is an excess of 5.11 km and 35.00% of optimal, so both limbs of the POL-RD-01 establishment test are satisfied: the excess is greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms. The route deviation the rider complains of is established on this trip's own trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02814", "EV-TRIP-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure the governing measurement and forbids citing the rounded trip-record copy for the threshold test. Here there is no conflict to resolve: the trace records 19.71 km and the trip record records 19.7 km, and the two agree to within rounding. The excess therefore stands uncorrected on either figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02814", "EV-TRIP-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is clean for policy purposes. It is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, carries 155 fixes at a 10-second sample interval with 100.0% coverage and no gaps, and its maximum gap is 0.0 seconds. POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is therefore not engaged, no independent corroboration is required and no ESCALATE is triggered under POL-RD-10(3).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: fare_model reads UPFRONT_QUOTE and quoted_fare_sgd is 21.50, so POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available however large the excess is. The rider's remedy is the POL-RD-11 route: the amount by which charged_total exceeds the quote, plus any properly chargeable pass-through lines. The establishment finding above is relevant to the record, but the money follows the upfront arithmetic, not a recomputed metered fare.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-11(a) arithmetic is fixed on this fare. charged_total is SGD 31.80, quoted_fare is SGD 21.50 and the properly chargeable pass-through and statutory lines total SGD 0.00, giving 31.80 less 21.50 less 0.00 = SGD 10.30, which the fare ledger publishes as pol_rd_11_remedy. That is the sum the rider is owed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "To be accurate about the quantum: the rider contested SGD 14.00, but the policy measures the remedy on an upfront-quoted trip as the excess over the quote, which on this fare is SGD 10.30. I do not contend for the balance of the contested figure, because POL-RD-11(a) does not provide for it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_over_quote",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing offsets that SGD 10.30. The fare carries zero ERP gantry lines (tolls_erp 0.00), no airport surcharge (0.00), and a waiting_time_fee of 0.00, so the properly chargeable pass-through total under POL-RD-09 is 0.00 and no statutory line reduces the refund. There is likewise no off-route or phantom gantry line to correct under POL-RD-09(4), and none is claimed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02814", "EV-GPS-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.properly_chargeable.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No rider-requested detour can be invoked against this claim. The chat log for this trip carries 0 messages, so there is no rider instruction that could meet POL-RD-04(a) to (c), no waypoint_hint to corroborate and no distance to exclude from the excess on that ground.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No endpoint amendment relieves the driver either. The trip record shows amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min both null and pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at both null, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run and no amended optimal route displaces the booked 14.6 km baseline.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not a pooled trip, so POL-RD-12 does not re-base the comparison. The trip record gives vehicle_type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null; the baseline is therefore the single optimal route of 14.6 km recorded at booking, and the co-rider exclusion has no application.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose that the traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-02814-01 is MISSING: it carries no payload, has admissibility status MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, and its issue code is MISSING_ARTIFACT. I cite it for the absence itself. Because no advisory covers this trip window, POL-RD-03 cannot be run, and no external traffic cause can be established on this record. The trace's own derived advisory block returns an empty advisory list against POL-RD-03, consistent with the missing artifact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02814-01", "EV-GPS-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's counterparty statement — 'The meter adds the extra distance' — names no evidence ID and invokes no clause. POL-RD-08 provides that an assertion which cites no evidence ID is discarded, and that once the rider has shown a matching trip and a threshold excess the driver must point to a specific artifact and a specific clause. This assertion points to neither, and on an upfront-quoted trip the 'meter' explanation is beside the point in any event, because the distance lines were fixed at booking.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02814", "EV-GPS-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider has discharged the initial burden under POL-RD-08. The trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all describe the same trip TRP-02814, the pickup event at 11:57:30 on 2026-08-10 is common to trace and trip record, and the excess of 5.11 km / 35.00% meets the POL-RD-01 threshold on an unimpaired trace. The burden has shifted to the driver and has not been discharged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02814", "EV-GPS-02814", "EV-FARE-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider profile adds no corroboration requirement to this claim. POL-RD-08's extra-corroboration factor applies only where deviation_claims_60d is 4 or more and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 1 or fewer; here deviation_claims_60d is 1. In any event the excess is 35.00%, above the 30% figure that factor speaks to, so the trace alone carries the finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02814", "EV-GPS-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The payment state matters to the ruling value. The fare ledger shows payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the rider is presently carrying the disputed over-charge. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION is party-relative and would leave that charge exactly where it is; only a refund under POL-RD-11(a) moves the SGD 10.30 back to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02814"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

