    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This was an upfront-quoted trip: EV-FARE-02814 carries fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE and quoted_fare_sgd 21.50. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-02814) measures 19.71 km between the recorded pickup and drop-off events against a booked optimal route of 14.6 km on EV-TRIP-02814 — an excess of 5.11 km, or 35.00% of optimal. That passes both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%), so the route deviation the rider complains of is established on this trip's own trace. It is NOT a MATERIAL deviation: 35.00% is below the 50% mark and 5.11 km is below the 8.0 km mark, so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not engaged in any event; and had it been, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d of 0 against 396 completed trips_90d establishes no repeat pattern, so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor the conduct referral is available. Because the fare was fixed at booking, POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however much longer the driven route was than the quote. The rider's remedy is POL-RD-11(a): charged_total SGD 31.80 less quoted_fare SGD 21.50 less the properly chargeable pass-through and statutory lines, which total SGD 0.00 here (no ERP gantry lines, no airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, waiting_time_fee 0.00) = SGD 10.30, already a multiple of 0.05. The rider contested SGD 14.00; the policy measures an upfront-quote remedy as the excess over the quote, so SGD 10.30 is the sum and the balance is not payable — the rider's own advocate did not contend for it. The driver's answer, 'The meter adds the extra distance', names no evidence ID and no clause, so under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and is discarded; it also misdescribes an upfront-quote fare, whose distance and time lines were fixed at booking. No rider-requested detour can be invoked (EV-CHAT-02814 holds 0 messages, so POL-RD-04 cannot run), no endpoint was amended (amended_optimal_distance_km, pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at all null, so POL-RD-05 cannot run), and this is not a pooled trip (vehicle_type RYDE_X, so POL-RD-12 does not re-base the comparison). The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02814-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and is cited only for its own absence: it carries no fact, no external traffic cause was asserted against it by any party, and it therefore triggers no escalation under POL-RD-10(5). The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (155 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s), so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) do not engage and no independent corroboration is required. Confidence is 0.90, capped at 1.0 by the deciding artifacts (EV-FARE-02814, EV-GPS-02814, EV-TRIP-02814), all at weight 1.0. One procedural note: the monetary effect of SGD 10.30 exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this provisional ruling issues but the amount is held for release by a human reviewer rather than executed automatically. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
