    "explanation": "This ruling concerns trip TRP-02814, a RYDE_X trip on 10 August 2026, quoted at SGD 21.50 and charged at SGD 31.80.\n\nTo the rider: the deviation you complain of is established. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02814) measures 19.71 km between the recorded pickup and drop-off events against the booked optimal route of 14.6 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02814) — an excess of 5.11 km, or 35.00% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (the excess is above 20% and above 0.8 km), and the trace is clean for policy purposes: 155 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, maximum gap 0.0 s, so POL-RD-07 is not engaged and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises.\n\nBut this is an upfront-quoted fare (fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE on EV-FARE-02814), so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02's metered recomputation does not run: your distance and time charges were fixed at booking, and the longer driven route costs you nothing on those lines. Your remedy is the amount by which the charged total exceeds the quote. The ledger gives charged_total SGD 31.80, quoted_fare_sgd SGD 21.50, and properly chargeable pass-through and statutory lines of SGD 0.00 (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00, airport_surcharge 0.00, waiting_time_fee 0.00). The refund is 31.80 less 21.50 less 0.00 = SGD 10.30, which is what the ledger publishes as pol_rd_11_remedy and the figure I award. It is less than the SGD 14.00 you contested; the balance is not something the upfront-quote rule measures, and your advocate correctly did not contend for it.\n\nTo the driver: your statement that 'the meter adds the extra distance' cites no evidence ID and invokes no clause, so it carries no weight under POL-RD-08; and it is beside the point here, because on an upfront-quoted trip the meter does not set the rider's price. No exculpatory route is open to you. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02814) holds zero messages, so POL-RD-04 cannot run and no rider-requested detour can be excluded. No endpoint was amended (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null; amended_optimal_distance_km is null), so POL-RD-05 cannot re-base the comparison. The vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02814-01 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and no external traffic cause is established on this record.\n\nOn conduct: the excess is 35.00% and 5.11 km, below both materiality marks (50% and 8.0 km), so this is not a MATERIAL deviation and POL-RD-06 is not engaged. Your profile would show no pattern in any event — deviation_flags_90d 0 against 396 completed trips in 90 days. No driver-conduct referral is produced, and none is produced under POL-RD-09(4) either, because the ledger carries no off-route or phantom gantry line and no surcharge on a trip that does not originate at an airport.\n\nConfidence is 0.9. The refund rests on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02814, weight 1.0), and the deviation on the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02814, weight 1.0) and trip record (EV-TRIP-02814, weight 1.0); the missing advisory is cited only for its absence and carries no fact. The monetary effect of SGD 10.30 exceeds the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling issues but is held for release rather than executed automatically."
